      "message": "[warning] Line 216: 🟡 `mergeContactMetadata()` persists each contact change immediately via `commitMetadata()-\u003esaveContactMetadata()`, and `saveContactMetadata()` rewrites the full contacts file. During syncs carrying many `ds.contact_metadata` entries, this becomes O(N * file_size) disk I/O and can significantly slow sync/apply paths. Prefer batching metadata merges under one lock and doing a single atomic save at the end (while still emitting per-contact notifications from the in-memory merged state).",
